# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-12-ethereumcreditguild/blob/2376d9af792584e3d15ec9c32578daa33bb56b43/src/governance/ProfitManager.sol#L409-L436


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The `ProfitManager` contract manages profits generated in the system and how it is distributed between the various stakeholders.

When a loan generates profit (interests) . This profit should have been distributed proportionally to GUILD holders who  have voted for the gauges, but a flaw in the `claimGaugeRewards` function could allow the profit to be stolen by malicious attackers.

## Proof of Concept
The claimGaugeRewards function code of the ProfitManager contract is as follows:
```solidity
function claimGaugeRewards(
    address user,
    address gauge
) public returns (uint256 creditEarned) {
    uint256 _userGaugeWeight = uint256(
        GuildToken(guild).getUserGaugeWeight(user, gauge)
    );
    if (_userGaugeWeight == 0) {
        return 0;
    }
    uint256 _gaugeProfitIndex = gaugeProfitIndex[gauge];
    uint256 _userGaugeProfitIndex = userGaugeProfitIndex[user][gauge];
    if (_gaugeProfitIndex == 0) {
        _gaugeProfitIndex = 1e18;
    }
    if (_userGaugeProfitIndex == 0) {
        _userGaugeProfitIndex = 1e18;
    }
    uint256 deltaIndex = _gaugeProfitIndex - _userGaugeProfitIndex;
    if (deltaIndex != 0) {
        creditEarned = (_userGaugeWeight * deltaIndex) / 1e18;
        userGaugeProfitIndex[user][gauge] = _gaugeProfitIndex;
    }
    if (creditEarned != 0) {
        emit ClaimRewards(block.timestamp, user, gauge, creditEarned);
        CreditToken(credit).transfer(user, creditEarned);
    }
}
```
The claimGaugeRewards function can be called by any user to claim  reward from a gauge, pay attention to the code:
```solidity
    if (_userGaugeWeight == 0) {
        return 0;
    }
```
When `_userGaugeWeight=0`, the `claimGaugeRewards` function will not continue executing and will not revert.

