# Vulnerability details

In `SurplusGuildMinter.sol` `getRewards()` is used to get rewards from a staking position, the variable `userStake` is first declared to reserve memory to hold a `UserStake` struct when the function is called, but the variable has not been initialised yet.
The variable is only initialised further down in the function 
```solidity
userStake = _stakes[user][term];
```

The issue here is that the variable `userStake` is used to determine if the user has been slashed or not before it has been `initialised` leading to its components being in their default values
```solidity
        lastGaugeLoss = GuildToken(guild).lastGaugeLoss(term);
        if (lastGaugeLoss > uint256(userStake.lastGaugeLoss)) {
            slashed = true;
        }
```
As `userStake.lastGaugeLoss` still has its default value of 0, if the `term` has ever suffered a loss in the past even before the user staked, the check will always return true (that is slashed will be set to true).


