# Vulnerability details

## Description

The ERC20MultiVotes  introduces a variable maxDelegates to limit the number of delegates an account can have. However, contracts can be exempted from this limit if canContractExceedMaxDelegates[contractAddress] is set to true. This exemption allows the contract to delegate votes to an unlimited number of accounts.

The functions transfer, transferFrom, and _burn call _decrementVotesUntilFree to ensure there are enough free votes to cover the token amount being transferred or burned. The _decrementVotesUntilFree function iterates over all delegates to free up votes.

## Proof

The vulnerability arises from the following code snippet in the _incrementDelegation function:

    bool newDelegate = _delegates[delegator].add(delegatee); // idempotent add
    require(
        !newDelegate ||
            delegateCount(delegator) <= maxDelegates ||
            canContractExceedMaxDelegates[delegator],
        "ERC20MultiVotes: delegation error"
    );

And the _decrementVotesUntilFree function:

    function _decrementVotesUntilFree(address user, uint256 votes) internal {
        // ... (omitted for brevity)
        for (
            uint256 i = 0;
            i < size && (userFreeVotes + totalFreed) < votes;
            i++
        ) {
            // ... (omitted for brevity)
        }
        // ... (omitted for brevity)
    }
## Impact
If a contract with permission to exceed maxDelegates delegates to a large number of accounts, the gas cost for iterating over these delegates in _decrementVotesUntilFree could exceed the block gas limit. This would make transfer, transferFrom, and _burn operations fail due to out-of-gas errors, effectively locking all funds in the delegating contract.



