# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Bad debts are easily created through under collateralised loans in the case of rapid market fluctuations.

## Discovery and Overview
The `LendingTerm` contract in the Credit Guild protocol employs a static variable `maxDebtPerCollateralToken` to determine the borrowing limit based on the collateral provided. This variable, once initialized, does not update to reflect market fluctuations in the value of the collateral versus the borrow token.

Currently to prevent borrowers from making under collateralised loan under price changes, it requires the GUILD token holders to propose an off boarding to the lending term, collect a quorum of votes, and finally make another function call to complete the off boarding. This process is most likely slower than completing a borrow, and vulnerable to frontrun attacks for risk-free profit -- make a borrow when seeing off boarding lending terms.

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Without changing the static borrowing limit design, the easiest fix is to add real-time price check of collateral token and credit token from oracles in `borrow` function.

